{"claim_id":"clm_scaling_broken_power_law_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"948120e47601e091","limitations":["has more free parameters to fit","reliable extrapolation needs data spanning the breaks"],"locator":"abstract","paper_id":"pap_scaling_broken_power_law","scope":{"domains":"vision_language_audio_rl_more","functional_form":"smoothly_broken_power_law"},"statement":"A smoothly-broken power law (BNSL), a product of power-law segments with smooth transitions, models and extrapolates scaling curves, including non-monotonic and sharply-inflecting ones, more accurately than a single unbroken power law.","tags":["broken_power_law","extrapolation","functional_form"]}
