{"claim_id":"clm_posenc_t5_relative_bias_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"315a76515b15e8f8","limitations":["bias is a scalar, no per-dimension position vector","no ablation isolating the bias in the abstract"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_posenc_t5_relative_bias","scope":{"architecture":"encoder_decoder_transformer","task":"text_to_text_transfer"},"statement":"T5 uses a simplified relative position bias: a single learned scalar per relative-position bucket is added directly to the attention logits, with buckets shared across all layers while each attention head learns its own set of biases.","tags":["relative_position_bias","learned_scalar","bucketed","layer_shared"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_posenc_t5_relative_bias_2","claim_type":"descriptive","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"898900f33dfe0985","limitations":["distant positions lose resolution by design","extrapolation quality not the paper's focus"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_posenc_t5_relative_bias","scope":{"architecture":"encoder_decoder_transformer"},"statement":"The relative position buckets use fine resolution for nearby offsets and coarser log-scaled resolution for distant offsets, so all offsets beyond a threshold map to a shared bucket, allowing the same parameters to apply at sequence lengths beyond training.","tags":["log_bucketing","relative_position","length_generalization"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_posenc_t5_relative_bias_3","claim_type":"descriptive","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"2e09e4db08da1056","limitations":["parameter savings, not accuracy, is the main advantage claimed","design choice within a large empirical study"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_posenc_t5_relative_bias","scope":{"task":"text_to_text_transfer"},"statement":"The scalar bucketed relative bias attains competitive quality while adding far fewer positional parameters than per-dimension position embeddings and sharing them across layers.","tags":["parameter_efficiency","simplification","shared_parameters"]}
