{"claim_id":"clm_posenc_alibi_2","claim_type":"predictive","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"fce7c4f82de6a513","limitations":["demonstrated on language-model perplexity","specific train/test length ratio"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_posenc_alibi","scope":{"model_size":"1.3B","task":"language_modeling"},"statement":"A model trained with ALiBi on sequences of length 1024 extrapolates at inference to length 2048 while matching the perplexity of a sinusoidal model trained directly at length 2048.","tags":["length_extrapolation","perplexity","train_short_test_long"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_posenc_alibi_3","claim_type":"descriptive","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"eb23b1a5271a9e66","limitations":["efficiency figures are for the compared configuration","measured on perplexity"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_posenc_alibi","scope":{"task":"language_modeling"},"statement":"Sinusoidal, rotary, and T5-bias position methods extrapolate poorly to longer inputs at inference, whereas ALiBi extrapolates while also training about 11% faster and using about 11% less memory than the sinusoidal baseline.","tags":["extrapolation_comparison","efficiency","positional_encoding_comparison"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_posenc_xpos_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"1781e313993c2344","limitations":["decay is an added inductive bias toward locality","decay rate is a design hyperparameter"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_posenc_xpos","scope":{"architecture":"decoder_only_transformer","task":"language_modeling"},"statement":"xPos augments rotary position embedding by multiplying the rotation with an exponential decay term along the sequence, damping long-distance token interactions to stabilize attention while preserving RoPE's relative-position property.","tags":["rotary","exponential_decay","relative_position","stability"]}
