{"claim_id":"clm_attn_flashattention_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"b53fad38cd1d760d","limitations":["benefit is tied to the asymmetric SRAM/HBM memory hierarchy of GPUs"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_attn_flashattention","scope":{"attention":"exact","hardware":"gpu"},"statement":"FlashAttention is an IO-aware exact-attention algorithm that uses tiling and recomputation to avoid ever materializing the full N-by-N attention matrix in slow GPU high-bandwidth memory (HBM), keeping intermediates in on-chip SRAM.","tags":["io_awareness","tiling","recomputation","exact_attention"]}
