{"claim_id":"clm_init_residual_fixup_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"b10b6aa804eb66f3","limitations":["Needs extra regularization to match normalized baselines."],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_init_residual_fixup","scope":{"arch":"residual_networks","normalization":"none"},"statement":"Fixup down-scales the weight layers inside each residual branch by a depth-dependent factor (roughly L^(-1/(2m-2)) for m layers per block), zero-initializes the last layer of each branch, and adds scalar multiplier/bias terms, so residual nets train with no normalization.","tags":["fixup","residual_scaling","depth_scaling","no_normalization"]}
