{"claim_id":"clm_init_residual_t_fixup_1","claim_type":"mechanistic","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"423adb9c8126773f","limitations":["Diagnosis validated mainly on translation-scale models."],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_init_residual_t_fixup","scope":{"arch":"encoder_decoder_transformer"},"statement":"In Post-LN Transformers the interaction of unbounded early updates with layer normalization produces large parameter-gradient variance near the output, which is the underlying reason learning-rate warmup is needed.","tags":["t_fixup","warmup","layer_norm","gradient_variance"]}
