{"claim_id":"clm_dynamics_lazy_training_1","claim_type":"mechanistic","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"48df0ee59fb29377","limitations":["formalized via a scaling limit","distinguishes cause but not all practical cases"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_dynamics_lazy_training","scope":{"cause":"large output scale factor","regime":"linearized dynamics"},"statement":"Lazy training, where a model reaches near-zero loss while its parameters barely move and it behaves like its linearization around initialization, is caused by an output-scaling choice rather than by over-parameterization per se.","tags":["lazy_training","linearization","scaling","over_parameterization"]}
