{"claim_id":"clm_dynamics_quantization_scaling_1","claim_type":"mechanistic","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"3f0cd0b4a7055ebf","limitations":["strongest validation on toy datasets","'quanta' extraction in LMs is approximate"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_dynamics_quantization_scaling","scope":{"hypothesis":"quantization hypothesis","mechanism":"ordered acquisition of discrete skills"},"statement":"Neural scaling laws can be explained if a network's knowledge decomposes into discrete 'quanta' (skills) learned in order of decreasing usage frequency, so a power-law (Zipfian) distribution over quanta-usage frequencies produces the observed power-law of loss versus model/data size.","tags":["scaling_laws","quantization_hypothesis","emergence","phase_transition"]}
