{"claim_id":"clm_recent_arch_yoco_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"5b831cde0341eb0a","limitations":["self-decoder uses efficient (e.g. sliding-window/linear) attention to bound its own memory"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_recent_arch_yoco","scope":{"cache":"single_global_kv","structure":"self_decoder + cross_decoder"},"statement":"YOCO is a decoder-decoder architecture in which a self-decoder produces a single global KV cache that a cross-decoder reuses through cross-attention, so key-value pairs are cached only once for the whole model rather than per layer.","tags":["decoder_decoder","kv_cache","cache_once","cross_attention"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_recent_arch_yoco_2","claim_type":"causal","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"db2ad160d156cee9","limitations":["gains largest for deep models and long contexts"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_recent_arch_yoco","scope":{"capability_kept":"global_attention","reduction_driver":"layer_count"},"statement":"Caching KV once reduces GPU memory demand by a factor that grows with the number of layers while retaining global attention capability.","tags":["memory_reduction","long_context"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_recent_arch_yoco_3","claim_type":"mechanistic","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"5816d27f25647e72","limitations":["prefill speedup specific to the two-stage layout"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_recent_arch_yoco","scope":{"benefit":"prefill_early_exit","context":"1M"},"statement":"Because the cross-decoder depends only on the self-decoder's global KV cache, prefilling can early-exit the self-decoder without changing the final output, significantly speeding up the prefill stage; YOCO scales to 1M context with near-perfect needle retrieval.","tags":["prefill_speedup","needle_retrieval","long_context"]}
