{"claim_id":"clm_recent_arch_gated_deltanet_1","claim_type":"mechanistic","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"400e88c40e9b2941","limitations":["requires a chunkwise parallel algorithm for hardware efficiency"],"locator":"method","paper_id":"pap_recent_arch_gated_deltanet","scope":{"mechanisms":"gating + delta_rule","target":"linear_attention_state"},"statement":"Gating and the delta update rule are complementary in linear-attention memory: gating enables rapid adaptive erasure of the state while the delta rule enables targeted key-value updates, and combining them (the gated delta rule) captures benefits neither achieves alone.","tags":["gated_delta_rule","linear_attention","memory_control"]}
