{"claim_id":"clm_r2_paramff_mixture_of_recursions_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"a36a21dc6dc775c1","limitations":["router adds a small learned overhead","requires training the routing jointly with the backbone"],"locator":"abstract","paper_id":"pap_r2_paramff_mixture_of_recursions","scope":{"components":["shared layer stack","per-token depth router","selective KV caching"]},"statement":"Mixture-of-Recursions combines two efficiency axes in one recursive transformer: it reuses a shared stack of layers across recursion steps for parameter efficiency, while lightweight routers assign each token its own recursion depth for adaptive computation.","tags":["recursive_transformer","weight_sharing","adaptive_computation","routing"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_r2_paramff_mixture_of_recursions_2","claim_type":"descriptive","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"f1783de370adb2a2","limitations":["demonstrated up to 1.7B parameters"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_r2_paramff_mixture_of_recursions","scope":{"budget":"equal training FLOPs","sizes":"135M-1.7B"},"statement":"At equal training FLOPs and smaller model sizes, MoR lowers validation perplexity and improves few-shot accuracy relative to both vanilla transformers and prior recursive baselines.","tags":["quality_per_parameter","perplexity","few_shot"]}
{"claim_id":"clm_r2_paramff_mixture_of_recursions_3","claim_type":"descriptive","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"c2445f297138797a","limitations":["throughput gains depend on the routed-token distribution"],"locator":"results","paper_id":"pap_r2_paramff_mixture_of_recursions","scope":{"mechanism":"selective KV caching for routed tokens"},"statement":"By caching key-value states only for tokens routed to deeper recursion, MoR raises inference throughput while cutting redundant attention compute and memory access.","tags":["inference_throughput","kv_cache"]}
