{"claim_id":"clm_r2_speed_scaling_law_lr_annealing_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"9cd2d26eadb7fefa","limitations":["empirical functional form","fit within a model/data family"],"locator":"abstract","paper_id":"pap_r2_speed_scaling_law_lr_annealing","scope":{"captures":"loss at every step, not just endpoint","models":"neural language models"},"statement":"The full cross-entropy loss curve under any LR schedule is captured by L(s) = L0 + A * S1^(-alpha) - C * S2, where S1 is the cumulative 'forward area' (sum of learning rates) and S2 is the 'annealing area' from LR decay.","tags":["loss_curve","scaling_law","lr_schedule"]}
