{"claim_id":"clm_r2_ngram_tensorizing_engram_1","claim_type":"method_definition","extracted_at":"2026-07-19","fingerprint":"2af67c30a2d7b467","limitations":["experiments limited to <=18-layer models","CP rank R must be chosen"],"locator":"abstract","paper_id":"pap_r2_ngram_tensorizing_engram","scope":{"factorization":"canonical_polyadic","param_scaling":"linear_in_rank_R","sharing":"across_ngram_orders"},"statement":"TN-gram replaces Engram's separate per-order hash tables with a shared Canonical Polyadic (CP) tensor factorization, using shared token-position factors plus order-absorption vectors so nested n-grams share latent structure, cutting scaling from O(V^n\u00b7d) toward O(n\u00b7V\u00b7R + d\u00b7R).","tags":["tensor_decomposition","shared_latents","hashed_ngram","parameter_efficiency"]}
